    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "tests: cover rejection of excessive 0xFF padding in DER integers",
    "user": {
      "login": "amartya1523",
      "id": 133855728,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOB_p58A",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133855728?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/amartya1523",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amartya1523/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`secp256k1_der_parse_integer` rejects a negative integer whose leading 0xFF byte is redundant (X.690 8.3.2), but nothing in the test suite checks it. `random_ber_signature` can produce such encodings, but doesn't mark them as `certainly_not_der`, so `run_ecdsa_der_parse` stays green if the check is removed, or if either of its two conditions is dropped (I tried all three; a coverage build also shows 0 hits on that branch).\n\nThis adds a small deterministic test with the padded encoding that must be rejected, plus the two neighbouring negative encodings that must still parse (as an overflow to zero): a lone 0xFF, and 0xFF 0x7F. It follows the same pattern as the recent long-form length test (#1924).",
    "labels": [],
