        }
      ],
      "message": "tests: cover rejection of excessive 0xFF padding in DER integers\n\nsecp256k1_der_parse_integer rejects a negative integer whose leading\n0xFF byte is redundant, but no test checks this. random_ber_signature\ncan produce such an encoding, yet it does not mark it as\ncertainly_not_der, so run_ecdsa_der_parse passes even if the check is\nremoved or either of its conditions is dropped.\n\nAdd a padded encoding that must be rejected, along with the two\nnegative encodings next to it that must still be accepted: a single\n0xFF byte, and a 0xFF byte followed by a byte without its top bit set.",
      "committer": {
