      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Thanks @pinheadmz , and sorry for the noise. Opening five PRs at once was too much and I’ve closed the other four.\r\n\r\nI kept this one because the excessive 0xFF padding check in secp256k1_der_parse_integer had no test: when I disabled it (or dropped either of its two conditions), the whole test suite still passed. E.g. FF 80 must be rejected because 80 alone already encodes -128, while FF (-1) and FF 7F (-129) are valid and should still parse (as overflow → zero). The new test checks exactly those three cases.\r\n\r\nI’ve read the AI policy. Going forward I’ll keep it to one PR at a time and wait for review. Happy to close this one too if it isn’t useful.",
